  "operative_text": "Section 1 (C.R.S. 18-12-603(1)): A PERSON SHALL NOT KNOWINGLY MANUFACTURE, IMPORT, PURCHASE, SELL, OFFER TO SELL, OR TRANSFER OWNERSHIP OF, OR KNOWINGLY CAUSE THE MANUFACTURE, IMPORTATION, PURCHASE, SALE, OFFER OF SALE, OR TRANSFER OF OWNERSHIP OF, AN ASSAULT WEAPON.\nSection 1 (C.R.S. 18-12-603(3)): AN ASSAULT WEAPON SHALL NOT BE SOLD OR TRANSFERRED BY AN INDIVIDUAL ON OR AFTER JULY 1, 2024, TO ANYONE WITHIN THE STATE, EXCEPT TO: (a) AN HEIR BY BEQUEST OR INTESTATE SUCCESSION; OR (b) A LICENSED GUN OR FIREARMS DEALER, WHO SHALL RENDER THE WEAPON INOPERABLE WITHIN NINETY DAYS OF THE TRANSFER.\nSection 1 (C.R.S. 18-12-603(4)(a)): AN INDIVIDUAL OR ENTITY THAT DOES NOT HAVE A PERMIT TO SELL FIREARMS BUT SELLS OR ATTEMPTS TO MAKE A PRIVATE SALE OF AN ASSAULT WEAPON IN VIOLATION OF SUBSECTION (1) OF THIS SECTION ON OR AFTER JULY 1, 2025, SHALL BE ASSESSED A CIVIL PENALTY IN THE AMOUNT OF SEVEN HUNDRED AND FIFTY DOLLARS.\nSection 1 (C.R.S. 18-12-604(1)): A PERSON SHALL NOT KNOWINGLY POSSESS A RAPID-FIRE TRIGGER ACTIVATOR.\nSection 1 (C.R.S. 18-12-605): A PERSON IS ENTITLED TO TRANSPORT AN ASSAULT WEAPON FOR ANY LAWFUL PURPOSE FROM ANY PLACE WHERE THE PERSON MAY LAWFULLY POSSESS AND CARRY THE ASSAULT WEAPON TO ANY OTHER PLACE WHERE THE PERSON MAY LAWFULLY POSSESS AND CARRY THE ASSAULT WEAPON, PROVIDED THAT THE ASSAULT WEAPON IS TRANSPORTED IN ACCORDANCE WITH THE FEDERAL REQUIREMENTS SET FORTH IN 18 U.S.C. SEC 926(a).\nSection 2 (C.R.S. 18-12-108.7(3)): Unlawfully providing a firearm, INCLUDING AN ASSAULT WEAPON, AS DEFINED IN SECTION 18-12-602, other than a handgun to a juvenile in violation of this subsection (3) is a class 1 misdemeanor."
}